rtla/timerlat: Exit top main loop on any non-zero wait_retval

jira KERNEL-1569
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-6.12.0-211.53.1.el10_2
commit-author Crystal Wood <crwood@redhat.com>
commit 3138df6f0cd04a75f8efa5b5270ba56d00a84ae6
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-6.12.0-211.53.1.el10_2/3138df6f.failed

Comparing to exactly 1 will fail if more than one ring buffer
event was seen since the last call to timerlat_bpf_wait(), which
can happen in some race scenarios.

	Signed-off-by: Crystal Wood <crwood@redhat.com>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20251112152529.956778-5-crwood@redhat.com
	Signed-off-by: Tomas Glozar <tglozar@redhat.com>
(cherry picked from commit 3138df6f0cd04a75f8efa5b5270ba56d00a84ae6)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

